@patterns.factory

Purpose:
  Object creation without specifying exact class.

UseWhen:
  - creation logic is complex
  - need to decouple creation from usage
  - multiple product families

AvoidWhen:
  - simple object creation with new
  - no variation in creation

Why:
  Centralizes creation logic and promotes loose coupling.

Related:
  @patterns.strategy

Examples:
  @project.payment
  @project.order

State: +
